Q: Is it possible to print non-printing characters with a %C specifier? A: <p>To expand on the answer by Aniket, you could use a combination of <a href="http://en.cppreference.com/w/c/string/byte/isprint" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><code>isprint</code></a> and the switch-statement solution:</p>
<pre><code>char ch = ...;

if (isprint(ch))
    fputc(ch, stdout);  /* Printable character, print it directly */
else
{
    switch (ch)
    {
    case '\n':
        printf(&quot;\\n&quot;);
        break;

    ...

    default:
        /* A character we don't know, print its hexadecimal value */
        printf(&quot;\\x%02x&quot;, ch);
        break;
    }
}
</code></pre>
